    {
      "text": "presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh, Matt. 2:11. if thou bring thy gift to the altar, Matt. 5:23. give good gifts unto your children, Matt. 7:11 (Luke 11:13; 3 Ne. 14:11). offer the gift that Moses commanded, Matt. 8:4. say to his father or his mother, It is a gift, Matt. 15:5 (Mark 7:11). sweareth by the gift that is upon it, he is guilty, Matt. 23:18. saw the rich men casting their gifts, Luke 21:1. on the Gentiles also was poured out the gift, Acts 10:45. God gave them the like gift as he did unto us, Acts 11:17. I may impart unto you some spiritual gift, Rom. 1:11. not as the offence, so also is the free gift, Rom. 5:15. by the righteousness of one the free gift came, Rom. 5:18. gifts and calling of God are without repentance, Rom. 11:29. gifts differing according to the grace, Rom. 12:6. come behind in no gift, 1 Cor. 1:7. diversities of gifts, but the same Spirit, 1 Cor. 12:4. covet earnestly the best gifts, 1 Cor. 12:31. though I have the gift of prophecy, 1 Cor. 13:2. desire spiritual gifts, 1 Cor. 14:1. Thanks be unto God for his unspeakable gift, 2 Cor. 9:15. minister, according to the gift of the grace of God, Eph. 3:7. Neglect not the gift that is in thee, 1 Tim. 4:14. tasted of the heavenly gift, Heb. 6:4. every perfect gift is from above, James 1:17. every man hath received the gift, 1 Pet. 4:10.",
